{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\fmodern Consolas;}}\uc1\pard\f0\fs18 # TagGroove licenses and third-party notices\par
\par
TagGroove application source is MIT licensed. Built-in audio fingerprinting links Chromaprint, FFmpeg, zlib and bzip2; non-Apple builds also use the KissFFT included with Chromaprint. Applicable component licenses and copyright notices follow. No GPL/nonfree/version3 FFmpeg components are enabled. A small recorded patch opts into upstream LGPL-marked audio components; exact original source, patches and build configuration accompany the matching release.\par
\par
The native regular-expression bridge also uses the vendored Boost.Regex library under BSL-1.0.\par
\par
The matching release provides complete corresponding application and native-library sources, build recipes and modification/relink instructions in `TagGroove-vVERSION-sources.tar.xz`. Obtain it from https://github.com/johnneerdael/TagGroove/releases . Library modification and reverse engineering for debugging modifications are permitted under the applicable library licenses.\par
\par
The application also displays these notices offline in Help > About TagGroove.\par
\par
