FFmpeg.\par
\par
Some optional parts of FFmpeg are licensed under the GNU General Public License\par
version 2 or later (GPL v2+). See the file `COPYING.GPLv2` for details. None of\par
these parts are used by default, you have to explicitly pass `--enable-gpl` to\par
configure to activate them. In this case, FFmpeg's license changes to GPL v2+.\par
\par
Specifically, the GPL parts of FFmpeg are:\par
\par
- optional x86 optimization in the files\par
    - `libavcodec/x86/flac_dsp_gpl.asm`\par
    - `libavcodec/x86/idct_mmx.c`\par
    - `libavfilter/x86/vf_removegrain.asm`\par
- the following building and testing tools\par
    - `compat/solaris/make_sunver.pl`\par
    - `doc/t2h.pm`\par
    - `doc/texi2pod.pl`\par
    - `libswresample/tests/swresample.c`\par
    - `tests/checkasm/*`\par
    - `tests/tiny_ssim.c`\par
- the following filters in libavfilter:\par
    - `signature_lookup.c`\par
    - `vf_blackframe.c`\par
    - `vf_boxblur.c`\par
    - `vf_colormatrix.c`\par
    - `vf_cover_rect.c`\par
    - `vf_cropdetect.c`\par
    - `vf_delogo.c`\par
    - `vf_eq.c`\par
    - `vf_find_rect.c`\par
