## External libraries\par
\par
FFmpeg can be combined with a number of external libraries, which sometimes\par
affect the licensing of binaries resulting from the combination.\par
\par
### Compatible libraries\par
\par
The following libraries are under GPL version 2:\par
- avisynth\par
- frei0r\par
- libcdio\par
- libdavs2\par
- librubberband\par
- libvidstab\par
- libx264\par
- libx265\par
- libxavs\par
- libxavs2\par
- libxvid\par
\par
When combining them with FFmpeg, FFmpeg needs to be licensed as GPL as well by\par
passing `--enable-gpl` to configure.\par
\par
The following libraries are under LGPL version 3:\par
- gmp\par
- libaribb24\par
- liblensfun\par
\par
When combining them with FFmpeg, use the configure option `--enable-version3` to\par
upgrade FFmpeg to the LGPL v3.\par
\par
The VMAF, mbedTLS, RK MPI, OpenCORE and VisualOn libraries are under the Apache License\par
2.0. That license is incompatible with the LGPL v2.1 and the GPL v2, but not with\par
version 3 of those licenses. So to combine these libraries with FFmpeg, the\par
license version needs to be upgraded by passing `--enable-version3` to configure.\par
\par
The smbclient library is under the GPL v3, to combine it with FFmpeg,\par
the options `--enable-gpl` and `--enable-version3` have to be passed to\par
configure to upgrade FFmpeg to the GPL v3.\par
\par
### Incompatible libraries\par
\par
There are certain libraries you can combine with FFmpeg whose licenses are not\par
compatible with the GPL and/or the LGPL. If you wish to enable these\par
libraries, even in circumstances that their license may be incompatible, pass\par
`--enable-nonfree` to configure. This will cause the resulting binary to be\par
unredistributable.\par
\par
The Fraunhofer FDK AAC and OpenSSL libraries are under licenses which are\par
incompatible with the GPLv2 and v3. To the best of our knowledge, they are\par
compatible with the LGPL.\par
